# Project Rules for mystudycosts.com (Bilingual MSC)

## Core Tech
- Framework: Next.js 15
- Styling: Tailwind CSS with dark blue theme
- State management: Zustand with persistence

## Mandatory Bilingualism (i18n)
- This project is strictly 100% bilingual: German (de) and English (en), implemented with `next-intl`.
- Never add a user-facing string as a hardcoded literal.
- Always update both `messages/de.json` and `messages/en.json` simultaneously when adding or changing UI elements.
- Ensure components support dynamic locale switching, including:
  - localized date/time formats
  - NC labels and terminology (e.g. "Zulassungsfrei" vs "Open Admission")

## UI Logic
- On NC-related pages/components, always include `NCDataDisclaimer` and provide the required `lastUpdated` prop.
- For any external or private university link/mention, use the `<AffiliateLabel />` component.

## Data Integrity
- When modifying NC data logic, follow and preserve the structure used by `scripts/update-nc-data.js`.
- For database tasks, respect dynamic schema probing and city field fallback logic (`city` -> `partner_city`).

## Communication Style
- Developer-facing communication: German.
- User-facing communication: fully localized according to current locale (German or English).

## Non-Negotiable Policy
- Zero Hardcoded Strings: all user-visible text must come from translations.
- Strict Bilingualism: every user-facing feature/change must be implemented in both German and English at the same time.
